package skill

// TraceResourceObservationContract is shared by raw-trace triage and trace
// query teaching. It describes source metadata without inventing producer
// semantics, execution spans, or causal claims. It is guidance only.
const TraceResourceObservationContract = "Native resource observation contract: NativeHook I markers are resource observations, not execution spans. Keep I resource-operation row counts separate from C counter-observation counts within the same requested scope; only report counts supplied by deterministic evidence. source_heap_size (resource-dependent units) is the per-event source quantity, not necessarily bytes or an allocation delta. HeapSize and MmapSize are independent cumulative snapshot series: C readings are not per-operation increments or decrements; do not merge different counter series or invent an initial zero. source_callchain_id (unresolved source key) retains its exact source integer; 0/-1 are not assigned stack or function meanings without the producer's contract. resource_end_ts_ns (NULL/0 do not prove release) retains the source end declaration; MaxInt64 and other positive values are not presumed sentinels, and do not subtract them to claim an execution duration unless the source contract establishes that meaning. Preserve decimal integers exactly, including values beyond floating-point integer precision; do not infer a floating-point encoding from their magnitude. Unresolved callchain keys do not identify functions. resource lifetime is not execution time, and resource observations alone do not establish a response-blocking causal chain."
